PLACEHOLDER - this is NOT a kallisto index.

A real hla.idx is a binary kallisto index built by `arcasHLA reference` (see
scripts/build_arcashla_reference.sh). This file exists only so that
`-profile test` satisfies `arcashlaReferenceDirExistsError()`'s check that
--arcashla_reference_dir points at a built reference rather than at an empty
or half-built directory. No test ever reads it: the tests that use this
directory either run `-stub-run` (where ARCASHLA_GENOTYPE's stub block never
invokes arcasHLA) or fail earlier, at parameter/samplesheet validation or at
ARCASHLA_VALIDATE_FASTQ.

See this directory's README.md.
